    "body": "I'll let @rashil2000 handle this since they're *much* more qualified than I am to deal with this. I would like to note briefly that the first bytes of the file do seem to (kind of) match what I expect. `hexyl` reports the following first two words of the file (posted aligned with the scoop output of `First bytes:`)\r\n\r\n```\r\nhexyl: 50 4b 03 04 14 00 00 00 ┊ 08 00 69 a2 95 53 a8 2b\r\nscoop: 50 4B 03 04 14 00 08 00\r\n                          ^ ???   ^ should be here?\r\n```\r\n\r\nI'm not sure if scoop condenses adjacent zero-bytes when reporting file output, but it seems you're at least getting the ZIP header and \"minimum ZIP version\" fields correctly.",
